.TH KBDANIM 1 "2026" "kbdanim 1.0.0" "kbdanim manual"
.SH NAME
kbdanim \- single-zone keyboard backlight animation engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kbdanim
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kbdanim
is a CLI-only, dependency-free Rust daemon and control tool for
single-zone RGB keyboard backlights exposed through the Linux
.I leds
sysfs class (typically
.IR /sys/class/leds/rgb:kbd_backlight ).
It drives 30+ real-time color and brightness animations, supports
presets and power-aware profiles, and can run either as a one-shot
foreground process or as a systemd user service.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run an animation in the foreground until Ctrl+C. Accepts all animation
options (see OPTIONS).
.TP
.B daemon
Run the animation engine as a foreground daemon, controllable via
.BR stop ", " status ", " mode ", " color ", " brightness ", etc.
Intended to be supervised by systemd (see systemd/kbdanim.service).
.TP
.B stop
Ask a running daemon to stop.
.TP
.B status
Show the running daemon's current mode, brightness, speed, etc.
.TP
.B restart
Stop the daemon (start it again yourself, or via systemd).
.TP
.B list
List every available animation with a one-line description.
.TP
.BI search " term"
Search animation names/descriptions for a substring.
.TP
.BI color " spec"
Set the LED color: a name, a
.B #rrggbb
hex code, an
.B r,g,b
triplet, or the literal
.BR random .
Applies to a running daemon if one exists; otherwise writes directly to
the device once.
.TP
.BI brightness " 0-255"
Set the global brightness.
.TP
.BI mode " name"
Change a running daemon's animation mode.
.TP
.B static
Set a fixed color (see
.B \-\-color
/
.BR \-\-brightness ).
.TP
.B off
Turn the keyboard LED off.
.TP
.BR gaming ", " night
Shortcuts for the built-in
.RI \[dq] gaming \[dq]
/
.RI \[dq] night \[dq]
presets.
.TP
.B preset list|run|create
Manage single-animation presets.
.TP
.B profile list|switch
Manage device-wide profiles (used for AC/battery auto-switching).
.TP
.B power\-profile ac|battery
Shortcut for
.BR "profile switch ac" / battery .
.TP
.B random\-mode on|off
Have a running daemon periodically switch to a random animation.
.TP
.B playlist run \fIname\fR
Cycle through a sequence of animations defined in a playlist file.
.TP
.B interactive
A simple line-based live controller (starts a daemon automatically if
none is running).
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose common device/permission/config problems.
.TP
.B config show|path|edit
Inspect or edit the configuration file.
.TP
.B completions bash|zsh|fish
Print a shell completion script.
.SH OPTIONS
These apply to
.BR run ", " static ", " gaming ", " night ", preset/playlist application,
and daemon startup where relevant.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " name"
Animation to run (default: rainbow). See
.BR "kbdanim list" .
.TP
.BI \-\-device " path"
LED sysfs directory (default: /sys/class/leds/rgb:kbd_backlight).
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " 0.1-10.0"
Animation speed multiplier (default: 1.0). Independent of
.BR \-\-fps ;
speed controls how fast simulated time advances, fps controls how
often it's recomputed.
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " 1-240"
Frames per second (default: 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-brightness " 0-255"
Global brightness (default: 200).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " spec"
Primary color: a name, #rrggbb hex, or r,g,b triplet.
.TP
.BI \-\-color2 " spec"
Secondary color, used by animations that blend or cycle between two
colors.
.TP
.BI \-\-easing " name"
One of: linear, smoothstep, ease\-in, ease\-out, ease\-in\-out, sine,
quadratic, cubic.
.TP
.BI \-\-period " seconds"
Base cycle/pulse duration; meaning varies per animation.
.TP
.BI \-\-randomness " 0-1"
How chaotic stochastic animations (fire, lightning, meteor, ...) feel.
.TP
.BI \-\-saturation " 0-1"
Color saturation knob.
.TP
.BI \-\-temperature " 0-1"
Warm/cool knob used by a few animations.
.TP
.BI \-\-intensity " n"
General intensity / flicker\-speed multiplier.
.TP
.BI \-\-palette " name"
A built\-in (warm, cool, fire, ocean, forest, sunset, cyberpunk,
pastel, monochrome, neon) or user\-defined palette.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " n"
Fix the RNG seed for reproducible stochastic animations.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity; repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only log errors.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kbdanim/config.toml
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kbdanim/presets/*.toml
User-defined presets.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kbdanim/palettes/*.toml
User-defined color palettes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kbdanim/playlists/*.toml
Playlist definitions for
.BR "playlist run" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kbdanim/state.toml
Persisted daemon state, restored on the next daemon start.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kbdanim/kbdanim.sock
Unix domain socket used for CLI-to-daemon control.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error (device, permission, config, or argument
errors are all reported on stderr with a description).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
kbdanim list
sudo kbdanim run --mode fire --speed 1.5
kbdanim daemon &
kbdanim status
kbdanim mode rainbow
kbdanim preset run gaming
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR udevadm (8)
.SH AUTHOR
kbdanim contributors.
